    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7aa44fa0_7b6f9666",
        "filename": "include/gpu/graphite/Context.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 155,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T16:57:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Tracing and logging could require making extra function calls at ever single trace/log call throughout our code. This can actually have a performance impact if the client is not using it. In this case, it is a call explicitly triggered by the client. If they never call this function there is near zero overhead.\n\nAs for release, this is often used by clients running release. For example on Android you can have a client dump out the gpu resources when trying to help debug an issue with an app. There device though will be running a release version. Same for Chrome and Chrome users.",
      "parentUuid": "030faabc_70704955",
